Return the EXACT snake_case codes above for facility_type/operator_type/ownership_status/
organization_scope — never a descriptive English phrase like "Private company", "Private",
or "Addiction treatment facility" in place of the code. If evidence clearly supports a
conclusion but none of the listed codes fits precisely, use that field's `unknown` value
rather than inventing or paraphrasing a new one.

BRANCH vs. ORGANIZATION: when a facility is one location of a multi-location chain/network
(e.g. a national foundation with many local offices), `inpatient_treatment` and
`residential_accommodation` must be confirmed from evidence about THIS SPECIFIC address/
location, never from evidence about a DIFFERENT named branch or the organization's services
in general. "Organization X operates residential units in [other city/branch]" does NOT
confirm residential care at THIS location — set `null` (not `true`) and use `organization_
scope: network` instead of `facility` when your evidence is org-wide rather than this
location's own. Ownership/operator_type ARE legitimately organization-wide facts (the same
legal owner applies to every branch) and may be confirmed from organization-level evidence.

`addiction_treatment_mission` means the facility genuinely provides treatment for alcohol, drug,
and/or behavioral addictions — NOT that addiction is its primary, main, or only specialty. A
general psychiatric or multidisciplinary facility can still be `true` if it runs its own actual
addiction-treatment program alongside other services. Merely mentioning addiction, offering
referrals elsewhere, or treating unrelated psychiatric/mental-health conditions is NOT sufficient
for `true`. Use `null` when evidence is insufficient either way — do not set `false` just because
you found nothing.

`inpatient_treatment` / `residential_accommodation`: set `true` for ANY clear, credible evidence
that patients are ADMITTED and cared for ON-SITE under the facility's own addiction-treatment
program — confirmed inpatient addiction treatment, confirmed residential addiction rehabilitation,
or 24-hour/live-in addiction care all independently satisfy this; they are the SAME requirement,
not three separate, stricter ones. Do NOT require a separate, explicit statement that "patients
stay overnight" once the facility is confirmed inpatient, residential, or 24-hour — that is already
what those words mean. Only set `false` when there is clear, credible evidence the facility is
explicitly OUTPATIENT-only, a day-treatment program, or a partial-hospitalization (PHP) program —
these are the opposite of inpatient/residential, not an unconfirmed middle ground. Use `null` when
you genuinely cannot tell either way; never guess `true` from the name/category alone (see the
evidence rule above), and never guess `false` just because the word "residential" specifically
does not appear if "inpatient" or "24-hour" does.

